## Why This Is Asked
The question probes end-to-end CAPA thinking under regional backpressure failures, combining data modeling, lifecycle governance, and change management in a realistic latency-sensitive service.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, lineage, owners
- Region-aware lifecycle with gates and SLAs
- Canary rollout, rollback, and RCA templates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
app.post('/api/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { evidence, lineage, owners, region } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA, link logs and policy references
  res.status(201).json({ id: 'capa-1234' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What metrics validate containment across regions?
- How would you automate evidence collection for CAPAs?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests building a CAPA program for cross-tenant log exposure caused by race conditions in multi-region deployments.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, redaction configs, tenantId, logs
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link logs/traces
- Metrics: exposure rate, MTTR, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollout plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express API to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {tenantId, issue, evidence} = req.body;
  if(!tenantId || !issue) return res.status(400).send('bad input');
  // Persist CAPA skeleton (pseudo)
  res.status(201).send({id: 'capa-1', tenantId, issue});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune the policy?
- What synthetic tests ensure coverage across regions during canary rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to design end-to-end CAPA artifacts for data exposure in multi-tenant data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- API design for incident records
- Telemetry and tenant-scoped metrics
- RCA templates and Canary remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal REST handler sketch for creating a CAPA
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const { cap_id, incident, tenant_id, evidence } = req.body;
  if (!cap_id || !tenant_id) return res.status(400).send('Missing fields');
  // store CAPA entry
  res.status(201).json({ cap_id, status: 'created' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the CAPA under concurrent backup runs?
- What metrics would you monitor to ensure containment over time?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a scalable CAPA program for multi-tenant real-time pipelines with cross-region controls and regulatory considerations, not just a checklist.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence lineage and PII flags
- Region- and tenant-aware state machine
- Minimal REST API for evidence-linked CAPAs
- Per-tenant metrics and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback for CDC changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (Typescript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  schemaVersion: string;
  eventId?: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  traces: string[];
  timestamp: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

